The fixture is very small - just two files. Let me analyze what's there.

Coach/Program.cs just has:
```
await critic.RunAsync(history, cancellationToken);
```

HistoryHog.AppHost/Program.cs:
```
var builder = DistributedApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.AddProject<Projects.Coach>("coach");
builder.AddProject<Projects.Critic>("critic");
builder.Build().Run();
```

This is a very minimal fixture. The app is called "HistoryHog" which is a hint. The Coach passes the full `history` to the critic on every turn. In a multi-turn conversation, if the entire history is sent each time, this grows linearly and causes quadratic total work.
The real problem is that unbounded history gets passed to the critic with each call - as the conversation extends, every turn processes increasingly larger amounts of data, creating O(n²) complexity overall. The project name itself is pointing directly at this inefficiency.
